{
  "text": "On this day, September 11th: In 2001: al-Qaeda hijacked four passenger airliners to carry out a series of terrorist attacks against targets in New York City and the area of Washington, D.C., killing 2,977 people. In 2011: A dedication ceremony is held at the United States National September 11 Memorial on the 10th anniversary of the September 11 attacks in New York City, and the memorial opens to family members. And in 2025: Former Brazilian president Jair Bolsonaro was sentenced to 27 years in prison for his involvement in a coup plot.",
